  "note": "Isaiah’s pools and Zephaniah’s capitals have encouraged identifications such as bittern and owl. None of the three verses describes plumage, spines or a diagnostic call. The Mandaic word may reflect contact with Arabic, and the Ebla comparison is tentative. The animal name alone cannot establish the origin of the verb."
